          "text": "{\"relation\":\"MATCH\",\"consensus_summary\":\"The eye chiefly symbolizes spiritual perception and inner moral condition; in specific idioms it signifies generosity versus stinginess, while God’s eyes signify omniscience, vigilance, and providential activity.\",\"book_summary\":\"The eye reveals inner light or darkness; a good eye is generous and an evil eye withholding; God’s fiery and multiplied eyes signify righteous, world-ranging watchfulness.\",\"consensus_core_identification\":\"Eye = spiritual perception or moral orientation, with established contextual senses of generosity/stinginess and divine watchfulness.\",\"book_core_identification\":\"Eye = manifestation of inner light or darkness, generosity or withholding, and God’s vigilant oversight.\",\"core_relation\":\"EQUIVALENT\",\"extension_relation\":\"SAME_CASES\",\"boundary_disagreement\":\"No material boundary disagreement. The book selects several standard contextual senses already identified by the consensus rather than denying other possible biblical uses. Its language about God’s eyes as “righteous watchers” shining like stars is an embellishment of the accepted vigilance imagery, not a clearly distinct core referent.\",\"material_contradiction\":\"None.\",\"rationale\":\"The book’s three main claims map directly onto consensus readings: Matthew 6 supports inner light and moral-spiritual condition; Proverbs supports the good-eye/evil-eye idiom of generosity versus stinginess; Zechariah and Revelation support divine vigilance and apocalyptic multiplied eyes. Differences are compression, emphasis, and poetic wording rather than replacement or reclassification of the central meanings.\",\"citation_support\":\"PARTIAL\",\"strongest_objection\":\"The printed citations strongly support the lamp, generosity/stinginess, fiery eyes, and world-ranging divine eyes, but they do not themselves state that the eyes “shine like the stars,” and “righteous watchers” is an interpretive personification rather than the explicit wording of the cited passages.\",\"confidence\":\"high\"}"
        }
